CodeBreaker's .NET metadata reader (this folder) is written from the ECMA-335 standard (Common Language Infrastructure,
Partition II). Its interface follows System.Reflection.Metadata (the names of its handles, row views, BlobReader,
SignatureDecoder, CustomAttributeDecoder, PEReader and MethodBodyBlock), so the port of ILSpy in dotnet/decompiler reads
like the original; custom_attribute_decoder.hpp, signature_decoder.hpp and pe_reader.cpp's method body reader follow
System.Reflection.Metadata's decoders decision for decision (dotnet/runtime, tag v9.0.0), so that values read as ILSpy
reads them.

